# Arbor versioning

**Product milestones** (Version 1, 2, 3 in `PROJECT.md`) describe eras of capability. **Package/git tags** (`v0.2.0`, `v0.2.1`, `v0.3.0`) track shipped releases.

## Rules

1. **`v0.2.0` = Version 2 complete** — automation and discoverability (jobs, FTS, watch, OCR, Word). The old single-column UI. Do not re-open v2 scope.

2. **Version 3 shipped as `v0.3.0`.** Work toward Version 3 shipped as **`v0.2.1`, `v0.2.2`, `v0.2.3`, `v0.2.4`, `v0.2.5`**. Package `v0.2.1` was the first step after Version 2.

3. **`v0.3.0` is the Version 3 completion package** — the features listed under Version 3 in `PROJECT.md` (shell, flashcards, quiz, concepts, diagrams, citations, cross-document linking, knowledge graph, embeddings, semantic search) and the 2026-10-17 Linux live run on the [implementation checklist](docs/implementation-checklist.md). Mac proof does not block the tag. The git tag is cut when the release lands. Two Notes constructs (tables, emphasis) were not in any live digest.

4. **Version 4 shipped as `v0.4.0`.** Work toward Version 4 shipped as **`v0.3.1`, `v0.3.2`, `v0.3.3`, `v0.3.4`, `v0.3.5`**. The 2026-10-18 Linux live run closed it. Issue #20 stays open until the parent closes it after `v0.4.0`. **Version 5 is in progress.** It ships as **`v0.4.1`, `v0.4.2`, …** until `v0.5.0`.

5. **CHANGELOG and package versions stay aligned** across worker, desktop, and Tauri (`python/src/arbor_worker/__init__.py`, `pyproject.toml`, `desktop/package.json`, `Cargo.toml`, `tauri.conf.json`). `arbor-worker --version` reads `__init__.py`.

6. **Version gates** live in [`docs/implementation-checklist.md`](docs/implementation-checklist.md). Local/VM tests gate every merge. A Linux live run gates the product-version tags (`v0.3.0`, `v0.4.0`, …). Mac batches are optional and never block a tag. Do not live-test every small feature. Do not start the next product version until the current version’s Linux live run is recorded.

7. **Version 6 is in progress.** It ships as **`v0.5.3`, `v0.5.4`, …** until `v0.6.0`. `v0.6.0` is the UI cutover (plan row 16). Do not tag `v0.6.0` before that row lands.

8. **Stay below 1.0.** Tags are `v0.MINOR.PATCH`. MINOR is the product version: Version N completes at `v0.N.0`. Every release on the way to the next Version bumps PATCH (`v0.5.36`, `v0.5.37`, …), features and fixes alike. Never tag `v1.0.0` or higher unless the owner asks for it. On 2026-11-01 every tag was renumbered: old major X became `0.X` with releases numbered in order (`v1.0.0` → `v0.1.0`, `v2.1.0` → `v0.2.1`, `v5.26.5` → `v0.5.34`, untagged 5.26.6 → `v0.5.35`; the old `v0.1.0`/`v0.2.0` pre-releases became `v0.0.1`/`v0.0.2`). Same commits. Plans and docs under `docs/` use the new numbers too; historical branch names such as `release/v3.0.0` keep their real names.

